# Build context is the repo root (see backend/Dockerfile), so exclusions must
# live here — backend/.dockerignore no longer applies to that build.
# Patterns are matched from the context root: use **/ for nested matches.

# VCS & tooling
.git/
.github/
.claude/
**/*.md
!README.md
# Markdown that is runtime *content*, not documentation. The agent prompt bodies and
# the RAG knowledge corpus are read from disk at runtime, so excluding them ships an
# image whose agents have no prompts and whose knowledge service ingests nothing —
# a silent quality failure rather than a startup error.
!ai/prompts/*.md
!ai/rag/knowledge/**/*.md

# Python
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.env
!**/.env.example

# Node / frontend (the backend image never needs these; ~400 MB of context)
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
frontend/

# Local data & artifacts
**/data/
infra/sandbox/__samples/
infra/sandbox/__output/

# Tests are not shipped in the runtime image
**/tests/
